From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:46:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 457/458] wifi: mt6797: join without a scan once the old link
 is down

A roam joins from an earlier scan's results. mac80211 takes the old link
down and adds the new station in one call, but a lifetime only opens when
a scan completes, so the station was refused and the supplicant had to
scan again. The channel also changed under the old link's teardown, whose
deauthentication still uses it.

Hold the last station removal until that teardown ends, wait for the
re-arm when the next station arrives, and open the lifetime a scan would
have left. Both waits are bounded at one second; a late end refuses that
join as before.

Part of the Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 4.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c   |   4 +
 .../net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac-priv.h   |   4 +
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c   | 153 +++++++++++++-----
 3 files changed, 123 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c
index 05dbc171a..61694b577 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c
@@ -2979,6 +2979,10 @@ int mt6797_mac_join_add_peer(struct mt6797_mac *mac,
 	int ret;
 
 	mutex_lock(&mac->mutex);
+	/* A roam joins from an earlier scan, as soon as the old link is down. */
+	mt6797_mac_join_await(mac, false);
+	if (!mac->scan_active && !mac->join_scan_ready)
+		mt6797_mac_join_open_lifetime(mac);
 	if (mac->scan_active || !mac->join_scan_ready) {
 		refused = (mac->scan_active ? BIT(0) : 0) |
 			  (mac->join_scan_ready ? 0 : BIT(1));
